{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"Epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"dysrhythmias\", \"id\": \"D001145\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"myocardial infarction\", \"id\": \"D009203\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"ventricular tachycardia\", \"id\": \"D017180\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"VT\", \"id\": \"D017180\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"VT\", \"id\": \"D017180\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"Epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"myocardial infarction\", \"id\": \"D009203\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"halothane\", \"id\": \"D006221\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"VT\", \"id\": \"D017180\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"Bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"VT\", \"id\": \"D017180\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"dysrhythmias\", \"id\": \"D001145\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"bupivacaine\", \"id\": \"D002045\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"epinephrine\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"Epinephrine","id":"D004837","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"bupivacaine","id":"D002045","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"dysrhythmias","id":"D001145","label":"Disease"},{"text":"myocardial infarction","id":"D009203","label":"Disease"},{"text":"ventricular tachycardia","id":"D017180","label":"Disease"},{"text":"halothane","id":"D006221","label":"Chemical"}],"head":"halothane","head_id":"D006221","pairs":[{"head":"Epinephrine","tail":"dysrhythmias","head_id":"D004837","tail_id":"D001145"},{"head":"Epinephrine","tail":"myocardial infarction","head_id":"D004837","tail_id":"D009203"},{"head":"Epinephrine","tail":"ventricular tachycardia","head_id":"D004837","tail_id":"D017180"},{"head":"bupivacaine","tail":"dysrhythmias","head_id":"D002045","tail_id":"D001145"},{"head":"bupivacaine","tail":"myocardial infarction","head_id":"D002045","tail_id":"D009203"},{"head":"bupivacaine","tail":"ventricular tachycardia","head_id":"D002045","tail_id":"D017180"},{"head":"halothane","tail":"dysrhythmias","head_id":"D006221","tail_id":"D001145"},{"head":"halothane","tail":"myocardial infarction","head_id":"D006221","tail_id":"D009203"},{"head":"halothane","tail":"ventricular tachycardia","head_id":"D006221","tail_id":"D017180"}],"relations":["D004837 | D001145","D004837 | D017180"],"result":"~","tail":"ventricular tachycardia","tail_id":"D017180","text":"Epinephrine dysrhythmogenicity is not enhanced by subtoxic bupivacaine in dogs. Since bupivacaine and epinephrine may both precipitate dysrhythmias, circulating bupivacaine during regional anesthesia could potentiate dysrhythmogenic effects of epinephrine. We therefore examined whether bupivacaine alters the dysrhythmogenicity of subsequent administration of epinephrine in conscious, healthy dogs and in anesthetized dogs with myocardial infarction. Forty-one conscious dogs received 10 micrograms.kg-1.min-1 epinephrine. Seventeen animals responded with ventricular tachycardia (VT) within 3 min. After 3 h, these responders randomly received 1 or 2 mg/kg bupivacaine or saline over 5 min, followed by 10 micrograms.kg-1.min-1 epinephrine. In the bupivacaine groups, epinephrine caused fewer prodysrhythmic effects than without bupivacaine. VT appeared in fewer dogs and at a later time, and there were more sinoatrial beats and less ectopies. Epinephrine shortened QT less after bupivacaine than in control animals. One day after experimental myocardial infarction, six additional halothane-anesthetized dogs received 4 micrograms.kg-1.min-1 epinephrine until VT appeared. After 45 min, 1 mg/kg bupivacaine was injected over 5 min, again followed by 4 micrograms.kg-1.min-1 epinephrine. In these dogs, the prodysrhythmic response to epinephrine was also mitigated by preceding bupivacaine. Bupivacaine antagonizes epinephrine dysrhythmogenicity in conscious dogs susceptible to VT and in anesthetized dogs with spontaneous postinfarct dysrhythmias. There is no evidence that systemic subtoxic bupivacaine administration enhances the dysrhythmogenicity of subsequent epinephrine.","metrics":{"precision":0.5,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.6666666666666666,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":1,"rel_fn":0}}